# Environment variables for xaviel-web-v2.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored — never commit real
# values. These are consumed by Vercel serverless functions under `api/` at
# runtime; they are NOT available to the Angular bundle, which is a static
# client build with no process.env.

# --- Contact form (existing, api/contact.ts) --------------------------------
# Resend API key used to send the contact-form email. Server-side only.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx


# --- Supabase / x-core ------------------------------------------------------
# The project URL and the anon key are NOT here on purpose. They are public-safe
# and live in `src/environments/environment.ts`, committed, the same way Music
# Hub carries them: the anon key identifies the project, RLS is what authorises
# (ADR-04). Putting them here would imply the bundle can read env vars. It
# cannot.
#
# The service_role key bypasses RLS entirely. It must NEVER appear in
# src/environments/, in any NG_/PUBLIC_-prefixed variable, or anywhere the
# browser can reach. Set it only where server code runs:
#   - Supabase Edge Functions (dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets), or
#   - Vercel project environment variables, for a function under api/
# Uncomment only if a server-side function in THIS repo comes to need it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Personal access token for the Supabase CLI, used by `npm run types:gen` and
# by `supabase db push`. Developer-machine only; not needed to build or deploy.
# Create at https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
